Dusk+ is a modified version of PolyPlus.

- PolyPlus 2.3.1 - https://github.com/Polyfrost/PolyPlus (commit c65c58b)
  By Polyfrost and contributors. GPL-3.0, see LICENSE.md.

Changes in this fork (November 2026), marked "Dusk:" in the source:

- Polyfrost's backend is not contacted. Accounts, the store, news, crash
  reporting and Epic Online Services are removed; the Epic classes left in
  network/eos are empty stand-ins so the rest of the code still compiles.
- Friends, messages, blocks, privacy, outfits and world hosting go through
  Dusk Client and its server (client/dusk: DuskBridge, DuskSocial,
  DuskHosting). Hosting uses e4mc.
- Parties, party voice, group chat and global chat are hidden until Dusk's
  server supports them. Voice settings no longer mention Epic.
- Right shift is left to Dusk Client's settings key: OneConfig's own key is
  moved off it on first start (client/dusk/DuskKeys).
- Config loading and the main-menu config hash were changed so a fresh
  install starts cleanly.
- The party invite button no longer shows while parties are off.
- Named "Dusk+", with Dusk's logos, wordmark, window title and menu text.
  Package names, mod ids, the built-in lobby scenes and the remaining
  artwork are still Polyfrost's.

Not affiliated with or endorsed by Polyfrost.

Dusk+ needs these at runtime. The Dusk launcher downloads them unmodified
from Modrinth; they are not part of this fork:

